#: ../../source/installation/installing_manual.rst:8
msgid ""
"The `CodeIgniter 4 framework "
"<https://github.com/codeigniter4/framework>`_ repository holds the "
"released versions of the framework. It is intended for developers who do "
"not wish to use Composer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/installing_manual.rst:12
msgid ""
"Develop your app inside the **app** folder, and the **public** folder "
"will be your public-facing document root. Do not change anything inside "
"the **system** folder!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/installing_manual.rst:16
msgid ""
"This is the installation technique closest to that described for "
"`CodeIgniter 3 "
"<https://codeigniter.com/userguide3/installation/index.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/installing_manual.rst:20
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/installing_manual.rst:22
msgid ""
"Download the `latest version "
"<https://github.com/CodeIgniter4/framework/releases/latest>`_, and "
"extract it to become your project root."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/installing_manual.rst:25
msgid ""
"Before v4.4.0, CodeIgniter autoloader did not allow special characters "
"that are illegal in filenames on certain operating systems. The symbols "
"that can be used are ``/``, ``_``, ``.``, ``:``, ``\\`` and space. So if "
"you installed CodeIgniter under the folder that contains the special "
"characters like ``(``, ``)``, etc., CodeIgniter didn't work. Since "
"v4.4.0, this restriction has been removed."
msgstr ""

